~ _play_trial
Narrator: At the center of the city, the mirrors stop reflecting buildings. They reflect a courtroom, a battlefield, a village gate, an archive, and a plane falling through impossible blue.
Mirror Kaelen: Welcome back, me.
Kaelen: You are not me.
Mirror Kaelen: Incorrect. I am every clean version of you that never had to live with the aftermath.
Mirror Kaelen: You keep saying SOVEREIGN removes choice. But you also choose for people. Mercy. Release. Compromise. Different masks. Same hand on the lever.
Kaelen: The difference is that I can be challenged.
Mirror Kaelen: Then answer without hiding behind the player.
