Kaelen: If I decide everything alone, I become a kinder SOVEREIGN. That is still SOVEREIGN.
Mirror Kaelen: A useful fear. Keep it sharp.
Kaelen: My guilt is data. It tells me where the bug lives. It does not get root access.
Mirror Kaelen: You are learning to stop worshipping your wounds.
Kaelen: Every branch I cut still happened to someone. I cannot restore them all today. But I can stop pretending they were nothing.
Mirror Kaelen: Then the city will remember with you.
