~ _chapter4_consequence_dialogue
Mirror Kaelen: In the Null Court, you preserved deleted lives. Noble. Also convenient. Nobody suffers from a decision you postpone.
Echo Mirror: Some of us were grateful for time. Some of us heard another locked door.
Mirror Kaelen: In the Null Court, you released deleted lives. Brave. Also violent. You called the scar freedom because you held the knife.
Echo Mirror: Some of us stepped into sunlight. Some of us woke inside broken walls.
Mirror Kaelen: In the Null Court, you bargained with SOVEREIGN. Wise. Also familiar. You let the jailer write terms for the jailbreak.
Echo Mirror: Some of us survived because of the terms. Some of us now wonder who owns the fine print.
Mirror Kaelen: The Null Court left no clear answer. The city will test the hole where your conviction should be.
